      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "islamophobia_hygiene_stereotype",
      "label": "Hygiene Stereotype Against Muslims",
      "description": "The meme implicitly references the stereotype that Muslims are unclean, by using the text 'pork is unclean?' and then sarcastically comparing it to goats, which are often associated with foul smell and uncleanliness in Western cultural perceptions. This stereotype is used to mock religious dietary practices (halal) and is a form of Islamophobia.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_dea7fe22"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_e36d51dd",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "vulgar_animal_insult",
      "label": "Vulgar Animal Insult",
      "description": "The phrase 'goat fuckers' is a vulgar, degrading insult that uses animal imagery to demean and insult. This type of language is often used in memes to provoke shock and laughter but can be deeply offensive and dehumanizing, especially when directed at religious or cultural groups.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
